---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LabEmailForm from '../components/LabEmailForm.astro';
import { network, forms, routes, founding, membershipContact, labApplicationSubject } from '../lib/network';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const hasEmail = Boolean(network.contact_email);
---

<Base
  title="Join as a lab"
  description="Join your lab through the GitHub form or email a completed application to Jixing Li, our membership coordinator."
>
  <h1>Join as a lab</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    {founding
      ? 'Labs in the Greater Bay Area and around the world are welcome. Labs outside the region can join as affiliates. Membership is by lab, and there are no fees.'
      : 'Membership is by lab and there are no fees. The principal investigator (PI), or someone with their agreement, submits a lab entry, which a coordinator reviews before publication.'}
  </p>

  <p>Choose either option below. The PI, or someone with the PI's agreement, can submit the lab entry.</p>
  <div class="join-options" aria-label="Two ways to join as a lab">
    <section class="join-option" aria-labelledby="join-github">
      <p class="option-number">Option 1</p>
      <h2 id="join-github">Join through GitHub</h2>
      <p>Fill in the GitHub lab submission form. <strong>A free GitHub account is required.</strong></p>
      <p class="small muted">Your submission creates a public issue. A coordinator reviews it before adding your lab.</p>
      <a class="btn primary" href={forms.lab}>Open GitHub form ↗</a>
    </section>
    <section class="join-option join-option-email" aria-labelledby="join-email">
      <p class="option-number">Option 2</p>
      <h2 id="join-email">Join by email</h2>
      <p>Fill in the email form and send it to <strong>{membershipContact.name}</strong>, our membership coordinator. <strong>No GitHub account is needed.</strong></p>
      {membershipContact.email ? (
        <>
          <p class="small muted"><a href={`mailto:${membershipContact.email}`}>{membershipContact.email}</a><br />{membershipContact.name} reviews new lab applications and helps prepare the listing.</p>
          <a class="btn" href="#email-form">Fill in email form ↓</a>
        </>
      ) : (
        <a class="btn" href={url('about/')}>Contact a coordinator</a>
      )}
    </section>
  </div>
  {membershipContact.email && <LabEmailForm name={membershipContact.name} email={membershipContact.email} subject={labApplicationSubject} templateHref={routes.joinEmail} />}

  <h2>Who can take part</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>Member lab</dt>
    <dd>A research group led by a principal investigator (PI) at an institution in the Greater Bay Area. Member labs appear in the directory and take turns hosting seminars.</dd>
    <dt>Affiliate lab</dt>
    <dd>A lab based outside the Greater Bay Area that takes part regularly. Affiliate labs appear in the directory with an affiliate label.</dd>
    <dt>Students, postdocs, research staff and other participants</dt>
    <dd>
      {network.mailing_list_url ? (
        <>You are welcome to take part without applying for membership. <a href={network.mailing_list_url}>Subscribe to the newsletter</a> for seminars, events, open positions and network news.
          Subscription is optional and needs no GitHub account.</>
      ) : (
        <>You are welcome to take part without applying for membership. <a href={url('events/')}>Browse the seminars</a>
          {hasEmail ? (
            <> and <a href={routes.followEmail}>ask to join the announcement list</a> for news about seminars, events and open positions. Check each event page or contact its host for joining details.</>
          ) : (
            <>. Contact a member lab for the announcement list and seminar joining details.</>
          )}
        </>
      )}
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>What is expected of a member lab</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>Hosting</dt>
    <dd>
      Member labs take turns hosting the monthly seminar, usually on the second Friday.
      With more labs than monthly slots, a lab's next turn may be more than a year away.
      If a date does not work, arrange a swap or deferral with the coordinators.
    </dd>
    <dt>Sharing</dt>
    <dd>Share useful learning resources, open positions and speaker suggestions. The forms are below.</dd>
    <dt>Confidential work</dt>
    <dd>No lab is expected to share unpublished data, research ideas, funding or other confidential material.</dd>
    <dt><a href={url('docs/code-of-conduct/')}>Code of conduct</a></dt>
    <dd>Everyone taking part in network activities, including coordinators, follows the code of conduct.</dd>
  </dl>
  <p class="small muted">
    Affiliate labs are not in the hosting rotation; participants who are not in a listed lab have no obligations
    beyond the code of conduct. The full text is in the{' '}
    <a href={url('docs/member-guidelines/')}>member lab guidelines</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How to add your lab</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      {membershipContact.email ? (
        <>Complete the <a href={forms.lab}>GitHub form</a>, or fill in the <a href="#email-form">email form</a> and send it to {membershipContact.name}.</>
      ) : (
        <>Open the <a href={forms.lab}>lab form</a>.</>
      )}
    </li>
    <li>Provide the PI's name, institution, city, up to eight research keywords and a short lab description. A photo is optional; initials are shown if no photo is supplied.</li>
    <li>
      Give consent. The entry's text is published under CC BY 4.0. A photo, if given, is displayed with your permission
      only and is not licensed for reuse.
    </li>
    <li>A coordinator reviews the entry and may ask for clarification. Approved entries appear in the lab directory.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Other ways to contribute</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt><a href={routes.nominateEmail || forms.nomination}>Nominate a speaker</a></dt>
    <dd>
      Anyone may suggest a speaker.
      {hasEmail ? (
        <> Nominations by email stay with the coordinators. The <a href={forms.nomination}>GitHub route</a> is a public issue.</>
      ) : (
        <> Coordinators review nominations. The form creates a public GitHub issue, so include only information you are comfortable sharing publicly.</>
      )}
    </dd>
    <dt><a href={forms.event}>Propose an event</a></dt>
    <dd>Suggest a seminar, workshop or summer school. See the <a href={url('docs/speaker-kit/')}>speaker kit</a> for the seminar format.</dd>
    <dt><a href={forms.tutorial}>Share a tutorial</a></dt>
    <dd>Share a notebook, course or recording. The website links to the material where its author hosts it.</dd>
    <dt><a href={forms.position}>Post a position</a></dt>
    <dd>Share PhD, postdoctoral, research assistant or faculty openings. Listings are removed after their closing or removal date when the website next updates.</dd>
  </dl>

  <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
    To change or remove an entry, write to the coordinators or edit its file by pull request. The rules are in the{' '}
    <a href={url('docs/charter/')}>charter</a>{founding && ', currently a draft for approval by the member labs'}, the{' '}
    <a href={url('docs/member-guidelines/')}>member lab guidelines</a>, the{' '}
    <a href={url('docs/code-of-conduct/')}>code of conduct</a> and the{' '}
    <a href={url('docs/privacy-and-consent/')}>privacy statement</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .join-options { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
  .join-option { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; min-width: 0; padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem); border: 1.5px solid var(--accent); border-radius: var(--radius); background: #f7f0ff; }
  .join-option-email { border-color: var(--ink); background: var(--soft); }
  .option-number { margin: 0 0 .75rem; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 750; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-strong); }
  .join-option h2 { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.3vw, 2rem); }
  .join-option p { margin-top: 0; }
  .join-option a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .join-option .btn { margin-top: auto; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .join-options { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
</style>
